  "problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\nI. The probability of getting $10$ ones on $25$ rolls of a biased $6$-sided die if the probability of getting one in a single roll is $0.4.$\n\nII. The probability of a student getting more than $10$ correct answers on a $20$-question test if the student has $60%$ probability of correctly answering each question.\n\nIII. The probability that a fair spinner with twenty-five regions, numbered from $1$ through $25,$ lands on seven more than $5$ times out of $100$ spins.",
